license: "Proprietary"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
abstract: >-
  PhoLine is a Chrome Manifest V3 research prototype that applies Christian
  Heinrich Hohlfeld's PhO-Compress Stage I to unchanged hosted LLMs. It filters
  linguistic redundancy on the client, places surviving meaning on a tokenizer-
  native English stem codebook, rewrites chat HTTP bodies before the tokenizer,
  and locally expands pilcrow-marked replies. IPA is used as a filter criterion,
  never as the wire payload.
keywords:
  - PhO-Compress
  - PhoLine
  - LLM
  - token compression
  - semantic compression
  - phonetic compression
  - browser extension
  - Christian Heinrich Hohlfeld
